o maintain an action against the master if the injury resulted from “deliberate intention” of the master to produce the injury, there must be a specific intent, not merely carelessness or negligent use of an agency after knowledge on the part of the master that it was dangerous and unsafe.</p>', 'headnotes': '', 'summary': '<p>Appeal from a judgment of the superior court for King county, Tallman, J., entered April 28,1921, upon granting a nonsuit, dismissing an action in tort.</p>', 'disposition': 'Affirmed.', 'history': '', 'other_dates': '', 'cross_reference': '', 'correction': '', 'citation_count': 8, 'precedential_status': 'Published', 'date_blocked': None, 'blocked': False, 'filepath_json_harvard': 'law.free.cap.wash.119/298.748318.json', 'filepath_pdf_harvard': 'harvard_pdf/4914801.pdf', 'arguments': '', 'headmatter': ''}]}], 'explanation': 'Citation found in CourtListener database', 'status': None, 'error_message': None, 'sources_checked': ['CourtListener Citation Lookup API']}
